<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ProvingGround.Pipeline.publish.xml — the estate-pipeline replica: it reproduces what the
  real deployment would do.

  STATUS: PLACEHOLDER — NOT YET VERIFIED AGAINST THE PIPELINE. The estate publishes through
  Azure DevOps -> Octopus with DacFx flags fixed in the pipeline's own XML. This file exists
  to hold those flags VERBATIM once they are recorded from the pipeline (with its DacFx
  version, pinned in ../../estate/toolchain.md). Until then it carries the production
  posture as proven in the Twin corpus — the block and smart-default axes shared with the
  Strict profile, and the production drop axis:

    BlockOnPossibleDataLoss = True   -> the locked gate; this pipeline cannot relax it.
    GenerateSmartDefaults   = False  -> no silent backfill.
    DropObjectsNotInSource  = False  -> the PRODUCTION drop axis: absence produces no drop.
                                        A removed file is a phantom — the object and its rows
                                        survive a green publish. Drops ship as explicit,
                                        ordered pre-deployment scripts.
    IgnoreColumnOrder       = True   -> column-order churn does not masquerade as a change.

  Use this profile to see the deployment-shaped outcome (phantoms included) on the disposable
  copy. Use Strict to make would-be drops visible. Neither replaces the other: Strict is the
  diagnostic posture, this is the deployment posture.

  To verify and promote this file from placeholder to replica:
    1. Record the pipeline's DacFx publish flags and version into ../../estate/toolchain.md.
    2. Mirror the flags here verbatim; note any axis that differs from this scaffold.
    3. Publish once against a disposable copy and confirm the trust outcome
       (is_not_trusted = 0 on a declarative FK add) matches the FINDINGS_AND_CHANGES.md
       Part 5 expectation for that DacFx version.
    4. Remove this STATUS banner and date the verification.

  Aimed only at the ProvingGround database on the warm container — a disposable copy of Dev.
  Never point this profile at anything real: a publish is a publish, whatever the posture.
-->
<Project ToolsVersion="Current" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetConnectionString>Server=localhost,11433;Initial Catalog=ProvingGround;User ID=sa;Password=Projection@Strong1;TrustServerCertificate=True;Encrypt=False</TargetConnectionString>
    <BlockOnPossibleDataLoss>True</BlockOnPossibleDataLoss>
    <GenerateSmartDefaults>False</GenerateSmartDefaults>
    <IgnoreColumnOrder>True</IgnoreColumnOrder>
    <DropObjectsNotInSource>False</DropObjectsNotInSource>
    <IncludeTransactionalScripts>True</IncludeTransactionalScripts>
    <AllowIncompatiblePlatform>False</AllowIncompatiblePlatform>
    <IgnorePermissions>True</IgnorePermissions>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
